                      <div class="modal-body"><div class="container-fluid"><div class="row"><div class="col-12 col-lg-4"><img src="/files/Uploads/head shot.png" alt="Katie Cramer" class="img-fluid" /></div>
                                <div class="col-12 col-lg-8"><p><strong>Position:</strong> Sierra Club North County Coastal Group Executive Committee</p><div><div><br></div><div>I am a marine conservation ecologist and lifelong environmentalist/outdoor enthusiast with over two</div><div>decades of experience at the interface of conservation science, policy, and advocacy. My scientific</div><div>research and advocacy efforts are guided by a desire to have a tangible, positive impact on nature and the communities that depend on healthy and intact ecosystems. Over the past decade, I have become very active with grassroots environmental advocacy within my local community, the City of Encinitas, where I have honed my community organizing skills and played a large role in the passage of several laws to improve the management and protection of our local environment.</div><div><br></div><div><span id="docs-internal-guid-51e8954f-7fff-a45c-d273-57b200bc4359"><div><span style="font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: Roboto, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;"><br></span></div></span></div></div></div></div></div></div>
